      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ]
        },
        "colorMode": "value",
        "graphMode": "none",
        "textMode": "auto"
      },
      "description": "Of those, nodes whose newest scan is younger than the scanner's own cadence, which is the same 7-day line PdctngCisScanStale fires on and Oldest Scan goes amber at. Tune `cis_scan_stale_days` to whatever your scan schedule actually is. It deliberately does not compare the scan against the last catalogue compile: evidence is older than the catalogue by construction, so that test answers zero on every estate.",
      "id": 1239822441
    },
