    {
      "title": "Expected-but-absent nodes, and the classification blind spot",
      "type": "text",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 7,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 28
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "**Not evidenced, and not one collector's fault.** Three rows the charter asks for have no metric behind them yet:\n\n- **Expected but Not Reporting** needs a source of truth outside PuppetDB, which pdctng does not have.\n- **Managed, Never Scanned** and **Scanned, Not Managed** need a per-node join between `resource_type_count` and the CIS scan family. `resource_type_count` is currently rendered as a fleet total with no `node` label, so the join cannot be built without changing what the collector emits.\n- **Missing Classification Facts** needs a node known to Puppet with no `environment` label on `puppet_node_info`, which by definition does not appear as a row anywhere Prometheus can query for it.\n\nParked here rather than built on a guess. Each is real follow-up work, not a rendering choice."
      },
      "id": 252920604
    },
